1B
).
The first release of the reference metabolome illustrates the metabolic diversity and complexity of each of the 153 plant species (Figure
1C
, and
Supplementary Table S3
). Notably, annotated metabolites are classified into eight groups, i.e. alkaloids, amino acid derivatives, flavonoids, lipids, nucleotides and derivatives, phenols, phenylpropanoids, and terpenoids. As an example, the reference metabolome of
Callistemon rigidus
is depicted in Figure
1D
. It contains MS1/MS2 data for all metabolites detected in
C. rigidus
, in both positive and negative ion modes, and, if available, annotation of the spectral features. Metadata can be found in the header section of the reference metabolome file (.msr or .mgf format). Like its reference genome, the reference metabolome of
C. rigidus
provides an essential reference for studies of its metabolism and physiology.
RefMetaPlant: a reference metabolome database and related toolset for plant metabolic research
Based on the reference metabolome constructed for plants of the five major phyla, we have developed and released the first version of a reference metabolome database for plants, RefMetaPlant. We use RefMeta for its abbreviation, to parallel with ‘RefSeq’, the reference sequence database at NCBI (
23
